<%# The reset flow's "form" state: new password with the strength meter and a
    confirmation.

    THE TOKEN. The mailed link is this page's address
    with the token after a "#", which no server is sent, so the page is drawn
    without one: the form hidden and its `token` field empty. The script
    (`reset-token`, controllers/reset_token_controller.js) moves the token
    from the address into the field, takes it out of the address bar and
    shows the form; with no token it shows the "incomplete" message instead.

    WHETHER THE LINK IS GOOD the page learns by asking once, as soon as it
    has the token (`check_url`, a POST with the token in its body): a link
    that is bad, used or lapsed goes to the "expired" state of the request
    page (`expired_url`) before anything is typed, and the fields are
    read-only until the answer is there. The rule is still the form's own
    request, which answers the same way.

    `@token` is set only on the 422 of a refused password, where the form
    comes back with the token it was sent with, so it is drawn open and
    nothing is asked again. Its alert is one line per message the service
    gave, never a sentence glued from them, and each password field says
    its own messages under it with the refused edge (`@field_errors`, by
    field); the field's messages are no live region, the alert is the one
    that is announced.

    Without JavaScript neither the form nor the message is shown, and the
    <noscript> line says why. A script that is on but never runs (a module
    that did not load) leaves the heading alone: the message is NOT drawn
    visible for that case, because everyone with a good link would see "This
    link is incomplete" until the script had connected.

    `autocomplete="off"` on the token field is not decoration: it keeps a
    browser from putting a value the script wrote back into the field on
    Back or a reload. %>
<% field_errors = @field_errors || {} %>
<div class="flex flex-col gap-[18px]" data-controller="reset-token"
     data-reset-token-check-url-value="<%= admin_check_password_path %>"
     data-reset-token-expired-url-value="<%= new_admin_password_path(expired: 1) %>">
  <%= render "admin/shared/auth_heading", title: t(".title") %>

  <%= render Admin::Ui::NoticeComponent.new(tone: :danger, size: :compact, id: "alert") do %><%= safe_join(Array(flash[:alert]).map { |message| tag.p(message) }) %><% end %>

  <noscript>
    <%= render Admin::Ui::NoticeComponent.new(tone: :danger, size: :compact, role: nil) do %><%= t(".noscript") %><% end %>
  </noscript>

  <%= form_with url: admin_update_password_path, method: :patch, class: "flex flex-col gap-[18px]",
        data: { reset_token_target: "form" }, html: { hidden: @token.blank? } do |form| %>
    <%= hidden_field_tag :token, @token, id: "reset-token", autocomplete: "off", data: { reset_token_target: "token" } %>
    <%= render Admin::Ui::PasswordFieldComponent.new(name: "password", id: "password", label: t(".new_password"), meter: true, autofocus: true,
          errors: field_errors[:password]) %>
    <%= render Admin::Ui::PasswordFieldComponent.new(name: "password_confirmation", id: "password_confirmation", label: t(".repeat"),
          errors: field_errors[:password_confirmation]) %>
    <%= render Admin::Ui::ButtonComponent.new(label: t(".submit"), type: "submit", class: "w-full", data: { password_submit: true }) %>
  <% end %>

  <%# The same shape as the request page's "expired" state: what is wrong,
      the way to a new link, the way back. %>
  <div class="flex flex-col gap-[18px]" data-reset-token-target="incomplete" hidden>
    <%= render Admin::Ui::NoticeComponent.new(tone: :danger, size: :compact) do %><%= t(".incomplete") %><% end %>
    <%= link_to t(".request_new"), new_admin_password_path, class: "#{setup_primary_button_class} w-full justify-center" %>
    <p><%= link_to t(".back"), admin_sign_in_path, class: Admin::Ui::ButtonComponent.classes(:tertiary, size: :small) %></p>
  </div>
</div>
